                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Performance: OS: Windows 7 64-bit  CPU: AMD FX6300 , GPU: GTX970 , RAM:8GB . \nThe game runs fine on my PC with steady 60 fps , never encountered a crash or any other problem so it seems at least for me that it is a good port.\n\nPros:\n- Lots of different character portraits to use ( they added more than operation abyss) . The exact number is 45 portraits if you use the basic mode unless you play classic mode which doesnt use character portraits.\n- Can use 2 blood codes instead of 1 ( for example you can have a warrior combined with a knight blood code. So this helps you use skills from both blood codes and increases your stats too )\n- 10 different blood codes for your squad including (Knight ,Mage, Priest , Academic ,Archer , Warrior , Samurai , Monk, Conjurer and Assassin)\n- Good Mouse and Keyboard support and you can also change the keyboard bindings.\n- Has endgame content.\n\nNeutral:\n- The game is difficult when you reach the final bosses and if you are not carefull or haven't leveled up before, they could kill most of your squad members with one hit.\n- UI is not simple enough and it was difficult to get used to. You might like it but I got easily lost many times.\n\nCons: \n- Some puzzles are very difficult to understand especially the ones in the beggining of the game .( I also left some MEMO if you get stuck on a puzzle they might help you)\n- The tutorial could be better. Also there is a ingame manual with a lot of information which explains many things but you will get confused with so many information so just read it if you get stuck on something.\n\n\n\n\nOverall the game was good for me and I can reccomend to people who like dungeon crawlers and for people who completed the first game. For me this game is one of the best dungeon crawelers we have on Steam ( Dont know about consoles)\n\nP.S (1): When you reach Shinobazu Prison sewers just go back and save your game. Trust me.\nP.S (2): If anyone is interested I recommend that at least in your squad you have a Knight(for the skill \"Aegis\" which protects your squad members) , Academic (can help you with hidden floors and traps) and a Healer. Without them I feel that the game would be very difficult.",
